So this isn't exactly the same as your suggestion, but I managed to access the videostream with GStreamer and OpenCV with the following command when initialising a camera:

```cpp
   // Define the Gstreamer pipeline
    std::string pipeline = "udpsrc port=5600 ! application/x-rtp,encoding-name=H264,payload=96 ! "
                           "rtph264depay ! h264parse ! avdec_h264 ! videoconvert ! appsink";

    // Open the video stream
    camera = cv::VideoCapture(pipeline, cv::CAP_GSTREAMER);
```

The [PX4 docs](https://dev.px4.io/v1.11_noredirect/en/simulation/gazebo.html#video) on video streaming helped a little too.

I now understand that connecting to the camera through the AutoPilot software is not used for streaming but rather for controlling basic camera functionality e.g. take photo etc. (though perhaps also streaming?) Video streaming was a little new to me but the above command should sort PX4 sitl issues out. 

@JonasVautherin, the inconsistent connection is definitely still a bit of an issue in general- perhaps due to heartbeat like you've suggested... not sure though.

